@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Mixed MVP / future. Retained broader-product associations require explicit future node labels; MVP uses only core/basic ProjectForge.
title MVP + EXPLICIT FUTURE PATHS — Logical concern dataflow across trust boundaries
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "Untrusted input domain" {
 rectangle "E1 Caller / external content source" as U
}
rectangle "Trusted application responsibility boundary" {
 usecase "P1\nValidate / establish attributable context" as V
 usecase "P2\nApply current owner authority / invariants" as A
 usecase "P3\nProduce permitted result / bounded metadata" as R
 V --> A : validated intent / context
 A --> R : actual scoped outcome
}
rectangle "Restricted state / secret domain" {
 database "D1 Owned state / pending intent / observations" as DB
}
rectangle "Restricted diagnostic domain" {
 database "D2 Sanitized evidence / telemetry" as LOG
}
U --> V : untrusted identifiers / content / credentials
A --> DB : guarded owned mutation / intent
DB --> A : current permitted state / observed effect
R --> U : bounded permitted result
R --> LOG : restricted metadata, not raw credential/content
legend bottom
 Ovals are data transformations, stores are logical; arrows carry data, not authority or control order.
 Trust boxes require actual validation/access/secret controls; they do not prove physical isolation.
 Provider/executor/target effect boundaries remain scoped in their owning designs.
endlegend
@enduml
